    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8d54f7d1_137c86c2",
        "filename": "block/blk-merge.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 870,
      "author": {
        "id": 1368904
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-25T19:20:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In kernel master all the elevator merge stuff has been removed and I think everything is now \"unified\" to use the functions in this file to merge bios/requests so this function is always called in master.\n\nIt also looks like the code to check whether bios/requests can be merged is split into blk_rq_merge_ok and blk_try_merge, with rq_merge_ok checking things like flags, and try_merge checking for \"continuity\", which is why I put the DUN continuity check here. We could put it in ll_new_hw_segments instead if it makes more sense for the check to be there instead.",
      "parentUuid": "a0f8934f_c05faf64",
      "revId": "fc8a42830e382302731d7eeb887396bcfccb0a02",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
